    "title": "Graco recalls select infant car seats over defect",
    "text": "Graco recalls select infant car seats over defect Video Player is loading.Current Time Duration Remaining Time ✕ Urgent recall you need to know about. Graco is recalling some of its snug ride, turn and slide car seats, and other products. They say they caught *** structural issue during post-production testing. So, screenshot this if you need to, I will give you *** beat, but these are the exact products and affected model numbers for this recall. You will see it is *** car seat, *** car seat base, and *** travel. System. Here's how to know if your product has been affected. You're going to look at the product label and find the model number, which is right here. If your product is included, Graco says to stop using the seat with the base immediately. You can still use the infant car seat without the base, following the instructions in the manual while you wait for *** replacement. Next, take *** Photo of the product label on the base showing the model number, date of manufacture, and the serial number. Then you're going to fill out this registration form on Graco's website and you'll upload that photo that you just took. Graco says it will give you *** replacement at no cost. Go click the link in our bio. We've included steps and links in the full story that is up on our website now. Graco is recalling some of its Snug-Ride Turn and Slide infant car seats after discovering an issue with the base of the model. Graco didn't say exactly what the problem is, but the company discovered it during post-production testing.The recall impacts models sold between January and March at Amazon, Target and Walmart.The company said that the car seats themselves are still safe to use, but parents should stop using the seat base. Owners of the recalled seats can contact Graco for a free replacement base.“We know parents rely on Graco products every day, and we understand this may create frustration and disruption for families. We are working quickly to support affected families and will provide a replacement product at no cost,” Graco said. According to Graco, the following SnugRide Turn and Slide products are being recalled:SnugRide Turn and Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat2231809 - Noir/Black2231887 - Sandstone/Tan2231806 - Mulberry/Girl-Plum2231885 - Sandstone/Tan2231881 - Noir/Black2231884 - Noir/BlackSnugRide Turn and Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat Base2231810 - BlackModes Nest Travel System with SnugRide Turn and Slide ICS2243083 - Noir/Black Graco is recalling some of its Snug-Ride Turn and Slide infant car seats after discovering an issue with the base of the model. Graco didn't say exactly what the problem is, but the company discovered it during post-production testing. The recall impacts models sold between January and March at Amazon, Target and Walmart.The company said that the car seats themselves are still safe to use, but parents should stop using the seat base. Owners of the recalled seats can contact Graco for a free replacement base.“We know parents rely on Graco products every day, and we understand this may create frustration and disruption for families. We are working quickly to support affected families and will provide a replacement product at no cost,” Graco said. According to Graco, the following SnugRide Turn and Slide products are being recalled: SnugRide Turn and Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat2231809 - Noir/Black2231887 - Sandstone/Tan2231806 - Mulberry/Girl-Plum2231885 - Sandstone/Tan2231881 - Noir/Black2231884 - Noir/BlackSnugRide Turn and Slide Rotating Infant Car Seat Base2231810 - BlackModes Nest Travel System with SnugRide Turn and Slide ICS2243083 - Noir/Black",
